[Music]  [Music]  hello youtube chess lovers my friends  this is gunjan here  welcome to my 45th episode of chess trap  series  just like kasparov if you love sacking  your queen  early in the opening then you come at  the right place  because in today's episode we are going  to look  at wonderful queen sacrifice line  against scandinavian defense from the  white perspective  the critical position arises after the  following opening move order  e4 d5 e captures d5  queen captures d5 and here it doesn't  matter  whether you are knight to c3 or knight  to f3 player  both leads to the same territory  so for example in this game white  continued with  knight to f3 and after the usual  response  bishop to g4 pinning down this knight  white indeed continued with knight to c3  not only attacking the queen but setting  up  a very small trap well  if black foolishly take on f3 then this  is the last time he is going to do it  as after the following sequence  knight captures d5 bishop captures deven  and now the sting in the tail knight  captures c7 check  which not only grabbed the rook in the  corner  but white obtained an exchange just  within  the seventh move of the game  so obviously bishop captures f3 is a big  time mistake  and that's why at this position the most  popular choice by the black cam  is queen goes back to his original place  okay now white claim in the center with  d4 and against this  although knight to f6 is one of the  popular choice  as per the online database there are  more than 30 games  continue with knight to c6  which at first sight looks the obvious  choice  because now black is indeed threatening  bishop captures f3  and then take on d4 something  not easy to defend for the white camp  well white has tried various responses  such as  bishop to e2 as well as bishop to b5  however white can set up a nasty trap at  this point  starting with d5  guess what all the game in the database  continue with knight to e5  putting more pressure on f3 knight  and obviously if white has to defend  this knight  then black has equalized the game  instantly  but nope here is the exact point  where our trap springs into the action  as white has this wonderful  queen sacrifice knight captures e5  bam  so not only grabbing a piece but  attacking that poor bishop  so black doesn't have any choice he has  to  accept this queen sacrifice but after  that  now white revealed his nasty idea  and i hope you already see it right  yup bishop to b5 check  well queen to d7 not only regained the  queen back  but gives wide a completely winning game  so the only critical move in this  position is  c6 counter-attacking the white bishop  okay we are going to take on c6  and now you see the beauty about this  position  white has two deadly discover check  and the most funny part is even though  black can see that one is coming he  can't  stop it  if bishop to e2 then obviously white is  in no hurry he will take this bishop  with his king so accordingly  as per the chess engine the baseline  goes as follow  a6 attacking the bishop  well no price for guessing white's next  move yup  c7 a discover check to the black king  and now after this forcing line  a captures b5 pawn captures d8  with a check black has to take with the  rook  but at the end when white gobble up  this bishop on d1 if you carefully  count the material even though  white has sacrificed his queen at the  end  he emerged with a peace advantage  that's it guys i hope you enjoy and  learn this  high profile queen sacrifice line in the  scandinavian  remember do not play any other moves  except d5 in this position and  when you open and continue with knight  to e5  you just give your opponent a root shock  with  knight captures e5 sacrifice your queen  but winning the game  thank you for watching this video feel  free to like subscribe and comment  and i will meet you in my next episode  very soon  bye and take care

